        "original_id": "1b1c5628-0508-5a33-8de2-e4fe20fe87ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Van Zant, Mick Jones, Allen Collins\n- Bands: Lynyrd Skynyrd, The Clash\n- Songs and Albums: “That Smell”, Street Survivors\n\nFacts:\n- Ronald Wayne Van Zant was born on January 15, 1948, and he became an American lead vocalist, primary lyricist, and founding member of Lynyrd Skynyrd.\n- Michael Geoffrey “Mick” Jones was born on 26 June 1955, and he became a British musician, singer, songwriter, cofounder, lead guitarist, and co-lead vocalist for The Clash.\n- Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins wrote the song “That Smell.”\n- The song “That Smell” was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.\n- Mick Jones remained with The Clash until his dismissal in 1983.\n- Ronnie Van Zant died on October 20, 1977.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
